<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 44,073 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 44,073 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 44,073 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 66,529 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			11,580	    8,583</p>
<p>    Import cargo			32,493	   57,946</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, four ships were expected to sail and nine were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 50,000	 Al Safa	     23/1</p>
<p>Naphtha		  11,000	 Trogir		23/1</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	   13,000	 Cielo-Di-Milano   20/1</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,000	 Stavros-1	   21/1</p>
<p>High speed diesel    27,300	 Chilham Castle    24/1</p>
<p>Sugar		     7,500	 Faurei		22/1</p>
<p>Gas oil		  56,000	 Keefan		22/1</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
